{"word": "booty", "source": "freedictionaryapi", "data": {"word": "booty", "entries": [{"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈbuːti/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈbʊu̯tʰɪi̯]", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈbuːɾi/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈbʊu̯ɾɪi̯]", "tags": []}], "forms": [{"word": "booties", "tags": ["plural"]}, {"word": "bootyn", "tags": ["alternative", "archaic"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(nautical) A form of prize which, when a ship was captured at sea, could be distributed at once.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Plunder taken from an enemy in time of war, or seized by piracy.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The soldier gets his booty ; the combatant his spoils ; the carnivorous animal his prey. Booty respects what is of personal service to the captor ; spoils whatever serves to designate his triumph ; prey includes whatever gratifies the appetite and is to be consumed.", "reference": "1818, George Crabb, English Synonymes Explained, in Alphabetical Order: With Copious Illustrations and Examples Drawn from the Best Writers, 2nd edition, London: Printed for Baldwin, Cradock, and Joy; and T[homas] Boosey, →OCLC, page 162:"}, {"text": "Hungry for fame and the approval of rare-animal collector Queen Victoria (Imelda Staunton), Darwin deceives the Captain and his crew into believing they can get enough booty to win the pirate competition by entering Polly in a science fair. So the pirates journey to London in cheerful, blinkered defiance of the Queen, a hotheaded schemer whose royal crest reads simply “I hate pirates.”", "reference": "2012 April 26, Tasha Robinson, “The Pirates! Band of Misfits”, in The Onion AV Club:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language